subgroups, written by the contributors) are licensed under the MIT License; see LICENSE.

That licence covers only what the contributors wrote. It does NOT cover, and this project does
not and cannot grant any right to, content retrieved at run time from third-party services:
paper titles, abstracts, full text, archive and dataset records, regulatory and clinical-trial
records, grant records, filings and headlines. Such content appears in

  digests/   the committed weekly digests: titles, links, detected entity names, counts and
             abstract excerpts of at most 420 characters
  data/      the SQLite database (metadata, abstracts, open-licensed sections and text, derived
             mentions) and its compressed snapshots, which the weekly and daily workflows publish
             as GitHub release assets (db-latest, db-YYYY-MM)
  .cache/    raw HTTP bodies of full-text fetches (local or on the CI runner; never committed)

