THIRD-PARTY DATA SOURCES

Terms as read on 2026-10-17; verify them before relying on this list. "Licence" below describes
the data, not this software. Rate limits are the documented ones; the HTTP client paces at or
below them (litradar/http.py).

  Europe PMC (EMBL-EBI)        EMBL-EBI Terms of Use. Article metadata is reusable. Full text is
                               taken only from the Open Access subset, where each article carries
                               its own Creative Commons (or similar) licence that travels with it.
                               No numeric rate limit is published; EBI asks users not to impede
                               the service for others.
  Crossref REST API            Bibliographic metadata is facts and reusable for any purpose;
                               Crossref states that some abstracts may be subject to publisher or
                               author copyright. Requests carry a mailto (polite pool).
  OpenAlex                     CC0 1.0 public-domain dedication. Abstracts are served as an
                               inverted index "for legal reasons" and reconstructed locally.
                               10 requests/s anonymous, 30 with a free key; per-account daily budget.
  NCBI: E-utilities, PubMed,   NLM/NCBI terms. NLM does not claim copyright on PubMed abstracts but
  PMC, GEO, SRA                publishers or authors may; NCBI places no restrictions on the use or
                               distribution of GEO and SRA data; PMC articles carry individual
                               licences. Requests identify tool and e-mail and stay within
                               3 requests/s (10 with a key).
  ENA portal API (EMBL-EBI)    EMBL-EBI Terms of Use; read-experiment metadata (accession,
                               instrument model, first_public).
  bioRxiv / medRxiv API        Author-selected licence per preprint (cc_by, cc_by_nc, cc_by_nd,
                               cc_by_nc_nd, cc0 or "no reuse"). The servers permit text and data
                               mining through the API and the TDM bucket, ask tools to link back
                               to the hosted text and forbid re-hosting; this software links and
                               never re-serves preprint text. No API rate limit is published.
  arXiv API                    Metadata CC0 1.0; full text stays under the submitter's licence
                               and is not fetched. One request every 3 seconds.
  Semantic Scholar API         API Licence Agreement; datasets ODC-BY 1.0 (attribution required).
                               1 request/s with a key.
  GDELT Project (DOC 2.0 API)  Open data: "unlimited and unrestricted use for any academic,
                               commercial, or governmental use"; the project asks for attribution.
                               The per-company news source, on by default (news.gdelt in
                               config/radar.yaml); headlines, links, dates and the matched company
                               only. GDELT asks for one request every 5 seconds; the client paces
                               at 5.5 s and skips the remaining companies after a persistent 429.
  SEC EDGAR                    US Government work, public domain. EDGAR fair-access policy: a
                               declared User-Agent with a contact address and at most
                               10 requests/s; the feeds are skipped when no contact is configured.
  openFDA                      Public domain (CC0) with the FDA's "unvalidated data" disclaimer;
                               results are not for clinical or regulatory decisions.
                               240 requests/min; 1,000/day per IP or 120,000/day with a free key.
  ClinicalTrials.gov API v2    US Government work, public domain; about 50 requests/min per IP.
  NIH RePORTER API             US Government work, public domain; one request per second.
  PRIDE Archive (EMBL-EBI)     EMBL-EBI Terms of Use; project-level metadata and instrument names.
  CZ CELLxGENE Discover        Curation API; dataset metadata only. Each collection carries its
                               own licence and publication link.
  Google News RSS              Google Terms of Service. news.google.com/robots.txt disallows the
                               /rss/ path to all agents, so this source is OFF by default and
                               opt-in only (news.google_news: false in config/radar.yaml; see
                               docs/LEGAL.md). When an operator turns it on: headlines and links
                               only.
  Journal and press RSS feeds  Publisher terms; headlines, DOIs and links only. Feeds that refuse
                               scripted access are dropped, not worked around.
  Unpaywall                    When queried, requests carry the contact e-mail; the same
                               open-access data is served by OpenAlex under CC0.

